THE A9 VERDICT AND THE EXIT STATUS OF THE SAME RUN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The census above is a reading taken from the artifact. The runner's OWN verdict
over the same file is a separate, mechanical statement, and it is recorded here
because a census that a human computed and a verdict that the runner computed
are not the same evidence:

  A9 POPULATION DEFECT lines emitted:  0
    (the runner's `a9_population_defect` fires on any MEASURAND column that
     fails the population check on a NON-MEASUREMENT cell -- n == 0 or
     empty > 0 -- and sets A9_OK=0. It fired on none of the 42.)
  STEP0C ADMISSIBILITY lines:          0   (none due; nothing failed)
  INSTRUMENT DEFECT lines:             0

  runner's terminal line, verbatim:

    RESULT: instrument sound; harness exit code 0.

  $ echo "EXIT STATUS: $?"
  EXIT STATUS: 0

  Read the exit status against the runner's own fork, so 0 is not taken as
  vacuous: an A9 failure on this path exits 1 (a blocking non-measurement
  population defect), an INSTRUMENT failure exits 9, and a clean run falls
  through to the harness's own code. 0 here is the clean fall-through, and it is
  the branch the 42 clean columns above predict.

  ONE FALSE START IS RECORDED RATHER THAN QUIETLY RETRIED, because a runner
  guard that fires is evidence about the runner. The first attempt at this
  re-capture exited 1 before starting anything:

    FATAL: data dir is NOT empty: <target>/spec356-smoke-data
           Each run needs its own fresh, empty dir -- retained frames from a
           previous run would answer this run's frame-kind census.

  That is the fresh-corpus guard refusing to let a stale corpus answer a new
  run's census. The repair was to remove the stale scratch dir -- never to
  relax the guard -- and the run above is the one that followed.

